---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# event_stream_lifecycle: one open thread's event stream across a serve
# restart, and the EventSource's terminal errors (go/tests/model/README.md).
# live_transcript_sync covers one serve with a non-empty ring and a
# channel-full drop; serve_restart_resume covers status and the banner.
# This flow is the transcript lines and the EventSource state machine
# when the serve behind the stream is replaced.
#
# Server (go/cmd/bough/serve.go serveForeground, internal/serve):
# - SIGINT/SIGTERM runs srv.Shutdown, which closes the listener and runs
#   the OnShutdown hook that cancels every request's context, so every
#   /events stream ends (its handler returns and unsubscribes). Only
#   then does the deferred sup.Close kill and reap the children. Until
#   the kill lands the child still runs and records entries to its
#   history file, and its reaper emits "exit" into a ring nobody is
#   subscribed to (supervisor.go Close, the reap goroutine in start).
# - NewSupervisor starts with empty events/seq/subs maps: serve B's ring
#   for the session is empty and its seq starts again at 1 until a child
#   of serve B records something.
# - GET /api/sessions/{id}/events answers 404 before any header for an
#   unknown session, and Guard answers 401/403 before the API; Last-Event-ID
#   is ignored, so a reconnect replays the whole (possibly empty) ring.
#
# Page (web/src/api.ts subscribe, web/src/app.tsx the `selected` effect):
# - subscribe sets only onmessage. EventSource on a network error (serve
#   down, connection refused) stays CONNECTING and retries on its own; on
#   a non-200 answer (a 502 from a reverse proxy such as `tailscale serve`
#   while serve is down, 404, 401, 403) it fails for good: readyState
#   CLOSED, an error event nobody listens to.
# - A recorded frame arms a 120ms catch-up, GET ?since=<last line's
#   history seq>. A failed catch-up shows "Updates paused" and re-arms on
#   a backoff; its Retry runs the catch-up now and nothing else (it never
#   re-subscribes). Only frames arm it: a stream that delivers nothing
#   (an empty ring) arms nothing.
# - The list poll refreshes the rows (status) but never the lines. It runs
#   every 12s instead of 4s whenever a thread is selected.
#
# Mapped states, as field values:
#   Idle_OPEN / TurnRunning        serve "a", es "open" (turn open|closed)
#   ShutdownBegun                  serve "draining", es "connecting"
#   TailWritten                    serve "draining", disk > lines
#   ChildKilled / ServeDown        serve "down" (the exit went into A's ring)
#   ServeBUp (empty ring)          serve "b", ring False
#   Reconnected_NoCatchUp          serve "b", es "open", not ring, not timer
#   NetworkDrop_Reconnected        es "connecting" -> "open" with ring
#   Non200 / ClosedForGood         es "closed"
#   SilentStale                    es "open", lines < disk, not timer, not paused
#   RowOnlyUpdates                 row == status, lines < disk
#   Resynced                       lines == disk
#
# Corrections to the mapped model, from the code:
# - SigTerm and ShutdownEndsStreams are one step: Shutdown closes the
#   listener and cancels the request context together, so the page sees
#   its stream end and its reconnects refused at the same time. There is
#   no step at which the stream is open while the listener is closed.
# - Delta is not modelled: a Seq-0 frame arms nothing and holds no line;
#   what it draws is live_transcript_sync's preview, not state here.
# - Delivery is folded into the Record that fans out (no channel here):
#   live_transcript_sync models the channel.
# - The poll slows (x3) whenever a thread is SELECTED
#   (`streaming = selected !== null`), not while a stream is open: the
#   page has no idea whether its EventSource is open. poll is "slow" in
#   every state of this flow.
# - 401 across a restart is not the common Non200: the token is read
#   from its file (serveclient.LoadToken), so serve B keeps it. The
#   common one is a proxy's 502 while serve is down, which makes the
#   fatal status reachable from a plain restart behind `--host`.
#   EventsNon200 is enabled in every state with the EventSource
#   CONNECTING, whatever the serve.
# - "No event fanned out after Close" holds by construction: the streams
#   unsubscribed at Shutdown, Subscribe refuses once closed, and Close
#   closes whatever subscriber is left. Here that is StreamsEndWithServe.
#
# Abstractions, to keep the graph small:
# - one session, one serve restart (A -> B). The turn is running under
#   serve A when the flow starts, with one entry recorded and shown.
# - disk is the count of history entries; lines is how many the page
#   shows. The page's lines are always a prefix of disk (catch-ups append
#   from the cursor, deduped by history seq), so a count is enough.
# - ring is only whether the serve's ring holds a frame for the session.
# - a catch-up is one step (sent and landed): live_transcript_sync
#   models the in-flight races. Backoff timing is not modelled.
# - NextPrompt's `-r` start on serve B also closes the dangling turn as
#   cancelled: two entries, counted as one.
#
# Fairness: the page's timers and EventSource retries, the list poll and
# the catch-up are strongly fair; Close and launchd's restart are weakly
# fair. The person (Retry, Reselect), the child (Record, Finish,
# NextPrompt), the signal and the network (SigTerm, NetworkDrop,
# EventsNon200) are not.
#
# PRODUCT GAPS. Four claims do not hold in the product. Each is written
# as the claim, with an exemption behind a GAP_* flag that names the
# gap. Setting the flag to False makes fizz fail with the trace in its
# comment; a product fix sets it to False and the spec must still pass.

MAXDISK = 3

# Serve B's ring is empty, so a reconnect to it replays nothing and arms
# no catch-up: the tail the dying child wrote between Shutdown and Close
# stays off the page until the next prompt or a reselect.
GAP_EMPTY_RING = True
# No onerror: a non-200 on /events closes the EventSource for good and
# the page still renders the thread live. Retry re-runs the catch-up but
# never re-subscribes, so nothing but a reselect or reload recovers it.
GAP_NO_ONERROR = True
# The list poll stays slow while a thread is selected, even when its
# stream is closed or connecting and delivers nothing.
GAP_SLOW_POLL = True

def status_of(turn, child):
    # internal/serve/status.go StatusOf, reduced: an open turn with a
    # live child runs, without one it was interrupted.
    if turn == "closed":
        return "done"
    if child:
        return "running"
    return "interrupted"

def up(serve):
    return serve in ("a", "b")

role Stream:
    action Init:
        self.serve = "a"        # a | draining | down | b
        self.child = True       # the session's child is alive
        self.turn = "open"      # open | closed (history)
        self.disk = 1           # entries on disk
        self.lines = 1          # entries on the page
        self.ring = True        # the current serve's ring holds a frame
        self.es = "open"        # EventSource: open | connecting | closed
        self.timer = False      # a catch-up is armed
        self.paused = False     # "Updates paused"
        self.row = "running"    # the status the page shows
        self.poll = "slow"      # list poll rate: slow (12s) | fast (4s)

    # --- the child (and the person's prompt) ---

    atomic action Record:
        # An entry recorded while serve A runs, or the tail the dying
        # child writes between Shutdown and Close (ChildWritesTail).
        require self.child and self.turn == "open" and self.disk < MAXDISK
        self.disk = self.disk + 1
        self.ring = True
        if self.es == "open":
            self.timer = True

    atomic action Finish:
        require self.child and self.turn == "open" and self.disk < MAXDISK
        self.disk = self.disk + 1
        self.turn = "closed"
        self.ring = True
        if self.es == "open":
            self.timer = True

    atomic action NextPrompt:
        # POST /prompt: ensure adopts the session (`-r`) when no child
        # holds it, else writes to the idle one.
        require up(self.serve) and (self.turn == "closed" or not self.child) and self.disk < MAXDISK
        self.child = True
        self.turn = "open"
        self.disk = self.disk + 1
        self.ring = True
        if self.es == "open":
            self.timer = True

    # --- serve ---

    atomic action SigTerm:
        require self.serve == "a"
        self.serve = "draining"
        if self.es == "open":
            self.es = "connecting"

    atomic fair action CloseKills:
        require self.serve == "draining"
        self.serve = "down"
        self.child = False

    atomic fair action ServeStart:
        require self.serve == "down"
        self.serve = "b"
        # Empty maps (NewSupervisor): no ring, and its event seq starts
        # at 1 again. The page never keys a line by that number (its
        # cursor is the last line's history seq): LinesNeverAhead and
        # LinesNeverShrink hold it to that.
        self.ring = False

    # --- network and the EventSource ---

    atomic action NetworkDrop:
        require self.es == "open" and up(self.serve)
        self.es = "connecting"

    atomic fair<strong> action EventSourceRetry:
        # Reconnect: the whole ring comes again (Last-Event-ID ignored).
        require self.es == "connecting" and up(self.serve)
        self.es = "open"
        if self.ring:
            self.timer = True

    atomic action EventsNon200:
        require self.es == "connecting"
        self.es = "closed"

    # --- the page ---

    atomic fair<strong> action CatchUp:
        require self.timer
        if up(self.serve):
            self.lines = self.disk
            self.row = status_of(self.turn, self.child)
            self.paused = False
            self.timer = False
        else:
            self.paused = True

    atomic fair<strong> action ListPoll:
        require up(self.serve) and self.row != status_of(self.turn, self.child)
        self.row = status_of(self.turn, self.child)

    atomic action Retry:
        # ThreadStripRetry: catch-up only, never a new EventSource.
        require self.paused
        if up(self.serve):
            self.lines = self.disk
            self.row = status_of(self.turn, self.child)
            self.paused = False
            self.timer = False
        else:
            self.timer = True

    atomic action Reselect:
        # Selecting the thread again (or reloading the page): the whole
        # transcript, a new EventSource, the ring replayed.
        require up(self.serve)
        self.lines = self.disk
        self.row = status_of(self.turn, self.child)
        self.paused = False
        self.es = "open"
        self.timer = self.ring

action Init:
    stream = Stream()

# No event reaches the page after Shutdown: the stream is never open
# against a serve that is draining or gone.
always assertion StreamsEndWithServe:
    return stream.es != "open" or up(stream.serve)

# Seq restart on serve B never merges or duplicates a line: the page
# never shows more entries than the file holds.
always assertion LinesNeverAhead:
    return stream.lines <= stream.disk

# ... and never drops one it showed.
transition assertion LinesNeverShrink(before, after):
    return after.stream.lines >= before.stream.lines

# Connected to a serve, the page is never short with nothing armed and
# nothing said. Gap: Reconnected_NoCatchUp on serve B's empty ring. With
# GAP_EMPTY_RING False fizz fails on SigTerm, Record (the tail),
# CloseKills, ServeStart, EventSourceRetry.
always assertion NoSilentStale:
    s = stream
    if not (up(s.serve) and s.es == "open" and s.lines < s.disk and not s.timer and not s.paused):
        return True
    return GAP_EMPTY_RING and s.serve == "b" and not s.ring

# A closed EventSource is shown as not live. Gap: no onerror. With
# GAP_NO_ONERROR False fizz fails on SigTerm, EventsNon200 (a proxy's 502).
always assertion ClosedIsSurfaced:
    return stream.es != "closed" or stream.paused or GAP_NO_ONERROR

# The list poll runs fast whenever no stream delivers. Gap: it slows for
# any selected thread. With GAP_SLOW_POLL False fizz fails on SigTerm.
always assertion PollFastWithoutStream:
    return stream.es == "open" or stream.poll == "fast" or GAP_SLOW_POLL

# With a serve up, the page eventually shows every entry on disk without
# a person's action. Gaps: the empty ring (stuck in Reconnected_NoCatchUp)
# and the closed EventSource (records never reach the page).
always eventually assertion ConvergesToDisk:
    s = stream
    if not up(s.serve) or s.lines == s.disk:
        return True
    if GAP_EMPTY_RING and s.serve == "b" and not s.ring and s.es == "open" and not s.timer:
        return True
    return GAP_NO_ONERROR and s.es == "closed"

# A fatal-status stream is eventually re-subscribed. Gap: no onerror, and
# Retry only catches up; only a reselect or reload makes a new one.
always eventually assertion FatalStreamRecovers:
    return stream.es != "closed" or GAP_NO_ONERROR

# "Updates paused" clears once serve is back.
always eventually assertion PausedClears:
    return not stream.paused
